                  <decoDesc>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d1"><locus target="#ir(ecto)" facs="001"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1012Equestrian">Equestrian Saint</ref> with caption <q>“Saint Filatawos”</q> (possibly a martyr) spearing an ox</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d2"><locus target="#iv(erso)" facs="002"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1035HolyMan">Holy Man Portrait</ref>,<persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4585Georgeo">St George of Lydda</persName> and the <term key="dragon" ana="#dragon"/> with a list of names written upside down</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d3"><locus target="#3v" facs="005"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1066DavidHarp">David Playing the Harp</ref> with captions <q>“King and Prophet David,”</q> and <q>“Harp.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d4"><locus target="#16r" facs="017"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1031VirginAndChild">Virgin and Child</ref> attended by the angels <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS7049Michael">Michael</persName> and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4377Gabriel">Gabriel</persName></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d5"><locus target="#30r" facs="031"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1035HolyMan">Holy Man Portrait</ref>,<persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4585Georgeo">St George of Lydda</persName> and the <term key="dragon" ana="#dragon"/> with captions <q>“Saint George,” and “dragon.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d6"><locus target="#49r" facs="050"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1049Resurrection">Resurrection of Jesus</ref> raising Adam and Eve. with captions <q>“Our Mother, Eve,”</q> <q>“How Our Lord Jesus Christ rose from the Dead on the Third Day,”</q> and <q>“With our Father, Adam.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d7"><locus target="#91r" facs="092"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1030Trinity">The Trinity</ref> with captions <q>“Holy Trinity,”</q> and <q>“with four creatures.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d8"><locus target="#109r" facs="110"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1067LastSupper">The Last Supper</ref></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d9"><locus target="#130r" facs="131"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1086StrikingHead">The Striking of His Head</ref> with caption right: <q>“Jesus Christ”</q> The patron reclines to the left: Caption: <q>“Yätnäbärǝḫ”</q> (a name which means, “Where have you been?”)</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d10"><locus target="#130v" facs="132"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1033Ascension">Ascension of Jesus</ref> with caption <q>“The Ascension of Our Lord, Jesus Christ.”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d11"><locus target="#131r" facs="132"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1012Equestrian">Equestrian Saint</ref> Alexander, riding an Eagle-horse toward the angel who guards Paradise</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d12"><locus target="#131v" facs="133"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1101GodFatherOrb"><seg corresp="AT1101GodFatherOrb">No item: AT1101GodFatherOrb</seg></ref> God the Father holding orb of authority in his left hand and his right hand raised in blessing. with caption <q>“How Father and Son. . .”</q></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="frame" xml:id="d13">
                    Decorative designs:
